# .clinerules — ADD Demo System (read before every task)

## Project
Firmware for the ADD Demo System: ESP32 (MKS DLC32 V2.1), PlatformIO,
**pioarduino = Arduino Core 3.x on ESP-IDF 5.x**. Contract: docs/CONTRACT.md.
Requirements (German): docs/Pflichtenheft_Demoanlage_ADD_Slim_V1.7.md.
Sprint plan and order: docs/Sprint_Prompts_Demoanlage_ADD_Slim_V2.md ("Sprint-Plan V3").
The task you get comes from docs/sprints/<Sprint>.md – do only that task.

## Hard rules
1. FROZEN files – never modify, rename or delete:
   - src/**/*.h (all headers), src/config.h
   - src/app/snapshot.cpp, src/app/command_queue.cpp, src/app/control_task.cpp
     (exception: Sprint I1 may fix compile errors in control_task.cpp – report every change)
   - everything in test/ and docs/CONTRACT.md
   - data/www/style.css, data/www/*.woff2, data/www/LICENCE-ubuntu-font.txt, scripts/fake_device.py
   - in skeleton files (src/display/display.cpp, data/www/*.html, data/www/app.js): everything that
     is not inside a function marked TODO for your task
   If a frozen file seems wrong: STOP and describe the problem. Do not work around it.
2. Implement exactly the functions declared in the headers. No extra public functions,
   no changed signatures, no new global variables visible outside a .cpp file.
3. src/logic/ is pure C++17: NO Arduino.h, NO ESP-IDF, NO FreeRTOS, NO heap allocation
   (no new/malloc/String/std::vector), NO static mutable state. It must build with g++ on the host.
4. ESP-IDF 5 APIs only. Forbidden IDF-4 leftovers: esp_task_wdt_init(timeout, panic),
   analogSetWidth(), <rom/crc.h>, legacy driver/i2s.h, ledcSetup()/ledcAttachPin().
5. Never use delay() or blocking loops in the control task or in logic. Never call Serial,
   NVS or the file system from the control task.
6. Code, comments and identifiers in English.

## Commands
- PlatformIO CLI:   pio  (symlink ~/.local/bin/pio -> ~/.platformio/penv/bin/pio).
                    Never use /usr/bin/pio, never install platformio via pip or apt.
                    If "pio" is not found: stop and tell the user (PATH problem).
- Host tests:       pio test -e native            (single suite: -f native/test_<name>)
- Quiet build:      pio run -e firmware -s          (complete firmware, from Sprint I1 on)
- Partial build:    pio run -e firmware-partial -s  (Sprints L1..H1: missing later modules are ok)
- JS tests (W1):    node --test test/js/test_app.js test/js/test_pages.js
- Frozen check:     git diff --exit-code master -- src/config.h ':(glob)src/**/*.h' test docs/CONTRACT.md data/www/style.css ':(glob)data/www/*.woff2' scripts/fake_device.py; echo "frozen $?"
                    must print "frozen 0". Otherwise undo YOUR changes to those files (they are not yours).
- NEVER run without explicit user approval: any "-t upload", "-t uploadfs",
  "pio test -e esp32-test", "pio device monitor". (Flashing can move the motor.)
- NEVER without explicit user approval: serial_cmd.py with a command that can move
  the axis or switch outputs: move, home, scan, stepper, slot, hv, shutter, beep,
  estop, sta. Allowed without approval (read-only): help, ver, crc, part, nvs, fs, uptime,
  in, watch, adc, adcraw, pos, disp, touch, wifi. "stop" is always allowed.
- NEVER without explicit user approval: git commit, git push, git tag, git reset,
  git checkout -- <file>, rm outside .pio/. The user commits and pushes.  
- Interactive tools hang the agent. For the serial port use:
  python scripts/serial_cmd.py "<command>" --timeout 10

## Definition of done (every sprint)
1. pio test -e native  -> all suites listed in the sprint are green (others may still fail
   only if their module belongs to a later sprint)
   REGRESSION RULE: every suite that was green before the sprint must still be green.
   Run the full native suite, not only the sprint suite.
2. pio run -e firmware-partial -s (L1..H1) or pio run -e firmware -s (from I1)
   -> no compile errors, no new warnings in your files
3. Frozen check prints "frozen 0" – run it yourself as the last step of every task.
4. Update the status table in README.md for this sprint: implementation status and
   test status (which suites are green, e.g. "test_safety_logic 52/52"), date.
   README.md is not frozen; never mark anything as done that is not green.
5. Report = copied tool output only (the lines the task asks for). No tables, no prose summaries,
   no numbers typed by hand. The reviewer only trusts output the user runs himself.

## Library knowledge
Read the real headers instead of guessing APIs:
.pio/libdeps/<env>/FastAccelStepper/src/FastAccelStepper.h and FastAccelStepperEngine.h,
.pio/libdeps/<env>/LovyanGFX/src/, .pio/libdeps/<env>/ArduinoJson/src/.
